In Test1, once you get an HTTP client, you can test the application by issuing an HTTP
request and then by analyzing the response returned by the application. More details on
how to process the response returned by the server will be given in the Use case section.
The next section explains how to test an application that runs in a controlled environment.
Testing a controlled application
In this case, we create an ASP.NET Core server within the test application and test it with
an HTTPClient instance. The Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing NuGet package
contains all that we need to create both an HTTP client and the server running the
application. We also need to reference the whole web framework by referencing
the Microsoft.AspNetCore.App NuGet package.
